WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · Internal Systems & Operations
Recap: Internal Systems & Operations

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your blueprint shows the systems you start with, who owns each and what comes next.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
You mapped how internal systems fit together and chose the minimum set you need to start well: processes, a planning calendar, people, finance and compliance essentials, information, tools and issue tracking.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:38.511
5.1 What a system is: your organisational operating map: A system is a repeatable way of doing necessary work, and the process comes before any app.

6
00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:48.630
5.2 Minimum viable systems by stage: Systems should be proportionate: built for the stage you are at, with clear triggers for the next.

7
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:59.378
5.3 Processes, SOPs and process ownership: Writing key processes down lets them be done consistently, safely and by more than one person.

8
00:00:59.778 --> 00:01:00.378
One lesson at a time

9
00:01:00.378 --> 00:01:09.756
5.4 The planning and reporting calendar: One calendar for all your planning, reporting and filing cycles prevents clashes and last-minute rushes.

10
00:01:09.756 --> 00:01:20.244
5.5 People and HR systems overview: People systems cover everyone’s journey with you, paid or unpaid, and your founders’ agreement is the first piece.

11
00:01:20.244 --> 00:01:31.733
5.6 Finance, procurement and internal controls overview: You need not start with every finance system, but should know which your form and plans require.

12
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:32.733
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:43.222
5.7 Compliance essentials from day one: If you will work with people, hold personal data, tell stories or handle money, some protections cannot wait.

14
00:01:43.222 --> 00:01:53.711
5.8 Information, documents and knowledge management: Deciding where files live, how they are named and who sees them is easiest before they pile up.

15
00:01:53.711 --> 00:02:05.570
5.9 Digital tools and the tech stack: Tools follow the process; a phone, a messaging app and a shared drive can be a complete stack.

16
00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:06.570
One lesson at a time

17
00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:17.689
5.10 Issues, actions and decisions tracking: Issues have already happened, unlike risks; keeping them in one place from the start makes patterns visible.

18
00:02:18.289 --> 00:02:30.519
Prove & Show starts with MEAL, turning your Theory of Change into evidence; later, Protect goes deeper into finance, legal compliance and risk on these systems.

19
00:02:31.119 --> 00:02:35.919
You check your Internal Systems Blueprint and download each exercise as a PDF.

20
00:02:37.419 --> 00:02:40.519
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
